From: howard-tran <howard-tran@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: Sort z -l results by descending score

Backport of upstream pull request #304 by howard-tran.

Display z -l results from highest to lowest score so the best matches appear
first.
---
diff --git a/z.sh b/z.sh
index c78f3cb..e4b8cf4 100644
--- a/z.sh
+++ b/z.sh
@@ -159,1 +159,1 @@
-                    cmd = "sort -n >&2"
+                    cmd = "sort -nr >&2"
